    <GaugingStation location="Partney Mill" name="Lymn" number="30004">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump weir gauging a rural catchment with mixed geology located in Lincolnshire Wolds, with minor artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">The weir is probably non-modular at very high flows due to backing up behind struts and a bridge, but is bypassed just before this point. Rated by model tests and confirmed by check gaugings to highest gauging of 0.6m. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Crump weir with 5m crest.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Station was bypassed in Oct 1993. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Abstraction for irrigation in upper reaches and some abstraction for PWS may have effect on low flows in summer.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Catchment with mixed permeability bedrock geology and some superficial deposits. Wholly rural, predominantly arable land use.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">PI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to within 26% of QMED. Good fit to available gaugings and flow remains modular." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="All flows are contained and remain modular to 2.4m. Rating expected to perform well to this point." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
